Problem Statement



Sharon is developing a Java program using in-built packages to manage a list of elements using arrays.



Initially, the array contains two elements: Apple and Banana. Sharon needs to:

Read an integer N (1 ≤ N ≤ 3) representing the number of new elements to add.
Read N strings from the user and add them to the array.


Finally, the program should display:

The original array elements
The updated array after adding all new elements


Help Sharon complete the program using arrays, Strings, loops, and Scanner only.

Input format :
The first line of input contains an integer N, representing the number of new elements to be added.

The next N lines each contain a string representing a new element.

Output format :
The first line of output prints "Original Array: Apple Banana"

The second line of output prints "Array after adding new elements: <all elements separated by space>"



Refer to the sample output for formatting specifications.

Code constraints :
1 ≤ N ≤ 3

1 ≤ length of each string ≤ 20

Strings contain only alphabetic characters (A–Z, a–z)

Initial array always contains: Apple Banana

Sample test cases :
    Input 1 :
        1
        Orange
    Output 1 :
        Original Array: Apple Banana
        Array after adding new elements: Apple Banana Orange

          
    Input 2 :
        2
        Grape
        Mango
    Output 2 :
        Original Array: Apple Banana
        Array after adding new elements: Apple Banana Grape Mango
